content.text:
I've sent the full inventory to the calling agent. I read the code only and changed nothing.

The findings that most affect building an admin server page:

- **Most customer actions already accept an admin.** Power, snapshots, backups, port forwards, firewall rules, files, game controls, services, databases and password reset all check "owner or role ADMIN". An admin who isn't impersonating can call them directly. Support and billing staff cannot.
- **Paid actions shouldn't be reused as-is.** Plan upgrades, disk expansion, dedicated IP purchase, volume ordering and backup-tier upgrades charge the caller's own wallet and are blocked while impersonating. An admin calling them would be charged themselves.
- **Admin-only actions that exist:**
  - suspend/unsuspend, extend, renew now, free toggle and grandfathered price, gated by `requireAdmin`;
  - reconcile, plus the admin backup, game-runtime and Admin Ops actions, gated by `requireArea("fleet")` (Admin Ops also blocks impersonation);
  - refunds, balance adjustments and card-health actions, gated by `requireArea("billing")`.
- **Dedicated IPs:** there is no RELEASE_DEDICATED_IP job type. Assigning, releasing and reassigning an IP all go through Admin Ops jobs (`startIpAssign`, `startIpRelease`, `startIpReassign`), which need a reason and a typed confirmation. Reverse DNS can only be set from the /admin/ips page (`setIpReverse`).
- **Things that don't exist:**
  - rescue mode;
  - a separate shutdown (stop is the only option);
  - a list-snapshots server action (the customer page calls the Proxmox library directly);
  - a CPU or network sample table (only memory, disk and daily uptime tables, plus bandwidth counters on the server);
  - a `lib/card-health` file (that logic is inside the card-health admin page);
  - any admin entry point for memory pinning (scripts and worker code only);
  - moving a VM (`VM_MOVE_ENGINE_AVAILABLE = false`).
- **Deleting a server** destroys the VM and every disk it owns, its volumes, dedicated IP, game DNS and the server record (a copy goes to `ServerArchive` first). I saw no step that deletes its stored backup archives.
- **Already admin-usable:** the file browser, VNC console and web terminal routes all accept an admin. The admin page does not show the root password today; the customer page does.
- **Off-site backup status** comes from `readPlatformBackups()`, which has no auth check. Any page using it has to gate itself.

The customer server page reads the tab from `?tab=`, so an admin can deep-link straight to a tab, e.g. `/dashboard/servers/${id}?tab=networking`. The report lists every tab for VPS and game servers.
